.Dd November 9, 2026
.Dt GLXINFO 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm glxinfo
.Nd show information about the GLX implementation
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Ss "SYNOPSIS"
.Bd -literal
     glxinfo [options]
.Ed
.Ss "DESCRIPTION"
.Bd -literal
     The glxinfo program shows information about the OpenGL and GLX
     implementations running on a given X display.

     The information includes details about the server- and client-side GLX
     implementation, the OpenGL and GLU implementations as well as a list of
     available GLX visuals.
.Ed
.Ss "OPTIONS"
.Bd -literal
     -v      Print visuals info in verbose form.

     -t      Print verbose table.

     -display display
             Specify the X display to interrogate.

     -h      Print usage information.

     -i      Force an indirect rendering context.

     -b      Find the "best" visual and print its number.

     -l      Print interesting OpenGL limits.
.Ed
.Ss "AUTHOR"
.Bd -literal
